{
  "_about": "laneVIS1 v1 (STAGED, not shipped). Read by the NEW Scripts/Zones/ZoneLook.cs (kit\\code\\ZoneLook.cs, UNCOMPILED). One global runtime Volume (priority 20) + by-name edits of the existing key / fill / rim lights + runtime local-fog boxes, all driven by the player's world z. enabled=false or an absent file = nothing. Switches i2 grade, i3 key+bounce light, i5 aerial perspective fog, i6 arena ground haze, i9 bloom+vignette, i18 hero rim. Args: -zonelook:off | -zonelook:2,3,9 (item list; wins over the switches) for same-exe A/B frames. -999 = inherit the default row. Row units: colorFilter linear rgb multiplier, postExposure EV (cancels the filter's luminance change), temperature/tint HDRP WhiteBalance -100..100, saturation/contrast ColorAdjustments -100..100, fogAlbedo volumetric albedo, fogTint = Fog.tint (colours the sky-derived far fog), fogMaxHeight/fogMeanFreePath = height fog (density kept equal at 2 m eye height), keyElevationDeg absolute sun pitch (-1 = leave), keyYawOffsetDeg added to the authored yaw, bounce = the existing FillCool directional (no shadows) re-coloured and re-aimed (-999 = keep authored aim), moonRimColor = MoonRim tint.",
